& =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot 5\\cdot 6\\cdot (-1)=-60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-60.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130292/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02e65c73-8c02-5403-8c5c-b1e81f81a7b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130292"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130320/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" :answer/id #uuid "c19aef0b-e255-5a99-bada-81072f5cc780" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130320/selection/25b335c1798b7b6a4cb13a35c15bf802d740cecd154b47b5e805a756e83b1528" :answer/id #uuid "52f82c4d-31e5-52d7-8fae-70e1d0308060" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130320/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "32b5e091-5aaa-5311-b5a7-4f8c4bda77ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130320/selection/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b" :answer/id #uuid "9946cd46-10a2-5252-8ce4-35ecc02cf6fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "44" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130320/selection/bc8ddfe9b0ae9ecd586464d3b828bfdd8a405438588d3184601cef690877fd8c" :answer/id #uuid "ea1bbb1a-b51e-51fa-b2dd-08ea39ccccbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-34" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130320/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "580425bc-0e3d-5c6f-9bdd-a25fdbe66342" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130320/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-130320/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" "q-130320/selection/25b335c1798b7b6a4cb13a35c15bf802d740cecd154b47b5e805a756e83b1528" "q-130320/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-130320/selection/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b" "q-130320/selection/bc8ddfe9b0ae9ecd586464d3b828bfdd8a405438588d3184601cef690877fd8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130320" :question/id #uuid "6cc689f5-55a8-5819-befb-256bf286c074" :question/math-academy-id "q-130320" :question/problem "Find the determinant of the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & \\,\\,\\,-4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,\\,-2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $3$rd row contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $3$rd row of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (3\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =-12\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-12(10-6) \\\\  & =(-12)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130320/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02e65c73-8c02-5403-8c5c-b1e81f81a7b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130320"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-69979/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "8e49e8c9-cb85-5740-b117-214bb26c1adc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69979/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "50f9d3ad-bfad-5817-8640-f48fb154ed9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69979/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "958992a9-ba88-55ea-a4e9-d153550bf044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69979/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "071ad2b8-d296-52de-a0ed-5b8d876b9ce8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69979/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "1afedeca-3d90-5b13-84f1-8788735547d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69979/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef00e8eb-fb0e-510e-a1ab-788708341000" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-69979/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-69979/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-69979/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-69979/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-69979/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-69979/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-69979" :question/id #uuid "e6db9f45-0830-59a7-8ba3-31125259ec1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-69979" :question/problem "Find the determinant of the matrix \n$G=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 6 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $4$th column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $4$th column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(G) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 13 & 6 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =(-2)\\cdot (1\\cdot 2\\cdot (-1))=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(G)=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-69979/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02e65c73-8c02-5403-8c5c-b1e81f81a7b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69979"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42486/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "39526073-07c5-5133-b375-93286b224999" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42486/selection/ebfc0e0786b9e08f32fe2539ae50e791a60b7c4613bb2a0820cefbd3ea742454" :answer/id #uuid "8c4dd01d-3fe3-5dc9-b8e4-8d5384f0e9b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42486/selection/5d34995cddd0166b343